Sonnet provides CMake targets:

    find_package(KF6Sonnet CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE KF6::SonnetUi KF6::SonnetCore)

Runtime setup is also required for spellchecking backends. Before the first
Sonnet use, register the directory containing kf6/sonnet with Qt:

    QCoreApplication app(argc, argv);
    QCoreApplication::addLibraryPath(pluginRoot);

For development, pluginRoot is <installed>/<triplet>/plugins for Release or
<installed>/<triplet>/debug/plugins for Debug. QT_PLUGIN_PATH can alternatively
contain that directory. Do not mix Release and Debug plugins or rely on files
remaining in vcpkg's packages directory.

For deployment, copy the contents of the matching plugins/kf6/sonnet directory
to <application-dir>/plugins/kf6/sonnet, deploy the matching Sonnet, Qt and
backend runtime dependencies, and register an executable-relative path:

    QCoreApplication::addLibraryPath(
        QCoreApplication::applicationDirPath() + QStringLiteral("/plugins"));

Do this after constructing the application and before constructing any Sonnet
objects. CMake target linking and vcpkg's app-local DLL copying alone do not
deploy these dynamically loaded backends. Check Sonnet::Speller::isValid() and
availableBackends()/availableLanguages() to diagnose missing backends or
dictionaries. Windows/macOS native backends need OS dictionaries; Hunspell
needs separately provisioned dictionaries.

With the qml feature, also add <installed>/<triplet>/qml (Release) or
<installed>/<triplet>/debug/qml (Debug) to QQmlEngine::addImportPath before
loading QML that imports org.kde.sonnet. For deployment, copy that module's
org/kde/sonnet directory and its runtime dependencies under
<application-dir>/qml/org/kde/sonnet, then use:

    engine.addImportPath(
        QCoreApplication::applicationDirPath() + QStringLiteral("/qml"));

Deploy the module's Qt Quick dependencies as well. QML import configuration
does not replace the backend plugin registration above.
